.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Aug 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-down - Take this machine off the AceTeam Network and restore routing/DNS


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel down [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reverses 'citadel up'.

.PP
If a 'citadel up' is running in another terminal, stop it there (Ctrl-C) so it
can shut down cleanly. This command is the recovery path for when that did not
happen — after a crash or a hard reboot — and removes any network interface
configuration, routes, and DNS settings left behind.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for down


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP
